<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jerónimo de Albuquerque Maranhão</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1548–<a href="/years/1618">1618</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jeronimo-de-albuquerque">Jerónimo de Albuquerque</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maranhao">Maranhão</a> was a Portuguese-Brazilian commander, son of Jerónimo de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-de-albuquerque">Albuquerque</a> of Pernambuco and a Tabajara mother. In 1614 he led the expedition against the French colony of Equinoctial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in Maranhão and defeated the French at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-guaxenduba">Battle of Guaxenduba</a>, leading to the surrender of Saint-Louis in 1615. He added Maranhão to his name and became the first captain-major of the region.</p></div>
